        "notes": "A 16-bar contrapuntal waltz-nocturne in D minor. Sections: A (bars 1-4, 4/4, pp, sparse half/quarter sighing motif), A' (bars 5-8, 3/4 waltz sway, p, motif sequenced and inverted), B (bars 9-12, 4/4 Agitato, mf, climax with octave-doubled melody and eighth-note arpeggios), A'' (bars 13-16, 4/4, mp to pp, augmented motif returns and cadences on D. Gradual transitions: bar 5 keeps a half-note bass under the new meter; bar 9 introduces the climax with an intermediate density before the peak in bar 11; bar 13 relaxes from mf to mp. The LH carries a real counter-line (not just pads) in bars 5-8 and 13-16. Tonal departure: bars 3-4 tonicize C major (VII) before returning to D minor."
